#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The test commands.

    scripts/test                      the fast checks (about a minute once built)
    scripts/test --all                every required check: the fast ones, the slow
                                      tests by exact name, the scripts' tests, the
                                      painter builds and the Python tests
    scripts/test --all --candidate C  test commit C in a fresh clean worktree and
                                      record a receipt (scripts/test_candidate)
    options: --summary FILE (JSON summary), --logs DIR (step logs; default a new
             directory under $TMPDIR), --list FILE (a step list other than the
             mode's), --only NAME (run the named steps of the list; the summary
             says so and its verdict is never "pass"), --phase build|check
             (only the build steps, or only the others; default both)

Two phases. The build steps run first, as one lockrun job of 600 s, then the
other steps as a second job of 600 s (the plan: builds and final check
batches, ten minutes each); the second runs only if every build passed. One
summary covers both, with each phase's limit, exit, verdict and time.
test_candidate runs the two phases itself (`--phase build`, `--phase check`)
under its pinned lockrun.

The steps are in notes/speed/test_lists/fast.tsv and all.tsv (reviewed lists,
protected in notes/golden_paths.txt; notes/speed/SKIPPED.md says what neither
runs, and why). No step replays a painting. Each line: kind, name, time limit
(s), the least number of tests it must run, a regex whose matching output
lines count as its tests ("-" for cargo and pytest, which report counts), a
bash command run from the repository root, optionally a group (or "-"), and
optionally a known failure in three more columns: an exit code, a regex and a
text. A step that exits with exactly that code, prints a line matching the
regex and has nothing else wrong is a known failure, not a pass: the run's
verdict is then "known_failure", shown as "NOT ALL GREEN (known pre-existing
failure: <text>)", exit 4 (the thinner's check 13 (b) awaits the user's
decision). Any other exit fails the step. A group:
consecutive steps of one group run at the same time, each with its own time
limit and its own TMPDIR (for steps that mostly wait, beside one that keeps the
cores busy). Kinds:

    build   a build; it has no tests (its time is reported as build time)
    cargo   `cargo test ...`: counts from the "test result:" lines
    pytest  counts from pytest's last line
    script  counts the output lines that match the regex

A list must hold at least one step that isn't a build, and every such step a
minimum of at least one test. A step fails if its command fails, it runs past
its time limit or it runs fewer tests than its minimum: a test name that
matches nothing fails. The run passes only if every step passes.

Locking and stopping. The whole run is one job of scripts/lockrun (600 s, the
plan's limit for builds and final batches), which validates any LOCKRUN_TOKEN
it inherits (a stale token waits for the lock like anyone). Every step runs in
that job's process group, so the outer timeout, a cancellation of lockrun and
a crash of this coordinator all reach every step still in the group (lockrun
stops the group and holds the lock until no process of it is left).

This coordinator stops only its own steps' processes. Each step runs with
CLAUDE_PAINT_TEST_RUN in its environment (the run's id and the step's); its
processes keep it when they leave the process group (the easel's session
server starts its own group), and no unrelated process has it. A step past
its limit is stopped with every process marked with its id, and every
descendant seen with it that is still in the group (repeated `ps` scans: a
child that outlives its parent is still known): SIGTERM, then SIGKILL until
none is left; the other steps of its group go on. After every step or group,
the run's leftovers are stopped the same way. When lockrun started this run
as its own job, any other process left in the job's group is a leftover too;
nested in another job (a batch, or test_candidate's lockrun) its other
processes are left alone. SIGTERM, SIGHUP or SIGINT to the coordinator stops
the running steps' processes and ends the run "unfinished" (exit 130). Not
stopped: shared daemons a step starts (sccache's server, which other jobs use);
a process that clears its environment and leaves the group; and, if this
coordinator is killed (SIGKILL), a marked process that left the group (lockrun
stops only the group).

Cargo's target directory is resolved once (`cargo metadata`: CARGO_TARGET_DIR
and Cargo configuration) and exported as CARGO_TARGET_DIR to every step, so
the steps that run `$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/easel` run the build just made.

Exit: 0 pass; 1 fail; 3 unfinished (a step timed out, or a partial run); 4 a
known failure and nothing else wrong; 124 a phase's lockrun timed out; 130
cancelled.

The summary (--summary) is JSON: mode, phase, verdict ("pass", "fail",
"unfinished" or "known_failure") and verdict_text, phases (when both ran), list (the list file, relative to the repository), list_sha256,
runner_sha256 (this file), target_dir, commit, whether the worktree was dirty,
wall seconds, the steps' build and test seconds (summed: grouped steps
overlap), and per step: name, kind, command, limit, least, group, exit,
seconds, tests_run, passed, failed, ignored, timed_out, ok, known_failure, known, why, log
and log_sha256. Exit 0 only on "pass".
"""

import argparse
import datetime
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time
import uuid

REPO = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
LISTS = {"fast": "notes/speed/test_lists/fast.tsv", "all": "notes/speed/test_lists/all.tsv"}
# the plan's limit for builds and final batches; scripts/tests/test_runner.sh may lower it
OUTER_LIMIT = 600.0


def git(*args):
    return subprocess.run(["git", "-C", REPO, *args], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()


def sha256(path):
    return hashlib.sha256(open(path, "rb").read()).hexdigest()


def read_list(path):
    steps = []
    for n, line in enumerate(open(path), 1):
        if not line.strip() or line.startswith("#"):
            continue
        f = line.rstrip("\n").split("\t")
        if len(f) not in (6, 7, 10):
            raise SystemExit("scripts/test: %s line %d: want 6, 7 or 10 tab-separated fields, found %d" % (path, n, len(f)))
        kind, name, limit, least, regex, cmd = f[:6]
        group = f[6] if len(f) >= 7 and f[6] not in ("", "-") else None
        known = None
        if len(f) == 10:
            try:
                known = {"exit": int(f[7]), "regex": f[8], "text": f[9]}
                re.compile(f[8])
            except (ValueError, re.error):
                raise SystemExit("scripts/test: %s line %d: a known failure is an exit code, a regex and a text" % (path, n))
            if kind == "build" or known["exit"] == 0 or not f[9].strip():
                raise SystemExit("scripts/test: %s line %d: a known failure needs a test step, a nonzero exit and a text" % (path, n))
        if kind not in ("build", "cargo", "pytest", "script"):
            raise SystemExit("scripts/test: %s line %d: unknown kind %r" % (path, n, kind))
        try:
            limit, least = float(limit), int(least)
        except ValueError:
            raise SystemExit("scripts/test: %s line %d: the limit and the minimum are numbers" % (path, n))
        if not 0 < limit <= OUTER_LIMIT:
            raise SystemExit("scripts/test: %s line %d: a step's limit is over 0 and at most %g s" % (path, n, OUTER_LIMIT))
        if kind != "build" and least < 1:
            raise SystemExit("scripts/test: %s line %d: step %s must run at least one test" % (path, n, name))
        if kind == "script" and regex == "-":
            raise SystemExit("scripts/test: %s line %d: a script step needs a regex to count its tests" % (path, n))
        steps.append({"kind": kind, "name": name, "limit": limit, "least": least,
                      "regex": None if regex == "-" else regex, "command": cmd, "group": group, "known": known})
    if not any(s["kind"] != "build" for s in steps):
        raise SystemExit("scripts/test: %s lists no test step (only builds, or nothing)" % path)
    names = [s["name"] for s in steps]
    if len(set(names)) != len(names):
        raise SystemExit("scripts/test: %s names a step twice" % path)
    # a group's steps must be listed together: they run at the same time
    seen, last = set(), None
    for s in steps:
        g = s["group"]
        if g is not None and g != last and g in seen:
            raise SystemExit("scripts/test: %s: the steps of group %r are not listed together" % (path, g))
        if g is not None:
            seen.add(g)
        last = g
    return steps


def count(step, out):
    """(tests_run, passed, failed, ignored) from a step's output."""
    if step["kind"] == "cargo":
        p = f = i = 0
        for m in re.finditer(r"^test result: \w+\. (\d+) passed; (\d+) failed; (\d+) ignored", out, re.M):
            p, f, i = p + int(m.group(1)), f + int(m.group(2)), i + int(m.group(3))
        return p + f, p, f, i
    if step["kind"] == "pytest":
        last = [l for l in out.splitlines() if re.search(r"\d+ (passed|failed|error)", l)]
        line = last[-1] if last else ""
        get = lambda w: sum(int(x) for x in re.findall(r"(\d+) %s" % w, line))
        p, f, e, s = get("passed"), get("failed"), get("errors?"), get("skipped")
        return p + f + e, p, f + e, s
    if step["kind"] == "script":
        n = len(re.findall(step["regex"], out, re.M))
        return n, n, 0, 0
    return 0, 0, 0, 0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- processes

# Every step runs with this variable in its environment: the run's id and the
# step's (inherited ids first, colon-separated). Its processes keep it whatever
# group or session they move to (the easel's session server leaves the group),
# unless they clear their environment; an unrelated process never has it, so a
# reused pid is never mistaken for a step's.
MARK = "CLAUDE_PAINT_TEST_RUN"
# Shared daemons a step may start but must not stop: other jobs use them too.
SHARED = {"sccache"}


def table():
    """{pid: (ppid, pgid, zombie)} of every process (ps works on macOS and Linux)."""
    ps = subprocess.Popen(["ps", "-A", "-o", "pid=,ppid=,pgid=,stat="], stdout=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)
    out = ps.communicate()[0]
    t = {}
    for line in out.splitlines():
        f = line.split()
        if len(f) >= 3 and int(f[0]) != ps.pid:  # (not ps itself)
            t[int(f[0])] = (int(f[1]), int(f[2]), len(f) >= 4 and f[3].startswith("Z"))
    return t


def marks():
    """{pid: (run and step ids in its MARK, its program's name)} of the processes that have MARK."""
    out = {}
    if os.path.isdir("/proc/self"):
        for d in os.listdir("/proc"):
            if not d.isdigit():
                continue
            try:
                env = open("/proc/%s/environ" % d, "rb").read().split(b"\0")
                argv0 = open("/proc/%s/cmdline" % d, "rb").read().split(b"\0")[0].decode("utf-8", "replace")
            except OSError:
                continue
            for e in env:
                if e.startswith(MARK.encode() + b"="):
                    out[int(d)] = (set(e[len(MARK) + 1:].decode("utf-8", "replace").split(":")), argv0)
        return out
    # macOS: ps -E appends each process's environment to its command line
    ps = subprocess.Popen(["ps", "-A", "-E", "-ww", "-o", "pid=,command="], stdout=subprocess.PIPE, text=True,
                          errors="replace")
    txt = ps.communicate()[0]
    pat = re.compile(r"(?:^|\s)%s=([0-9a-f.:]+)(?=\s|$)" % MARK)
    for line in txt.splitlines():
        m = pat.search(line)
        f = line.split(None, 2)
        if m and len(f) >= 2 and int(f[0]) != ps.pid:
            out[int(f[0])] = (set(m.group(1).split(":")), f[1])
    return out


def descendants(root, t):
    kids = {}
    for pid, (ppid, _, _) in t.items():
        kids.setdefault(ppid, []).append(pid)
    out, todo = set(), [root]
    while todo:
        for k in kids.get(todo.pop(), []):
            if k not in out:
                out.add(k)
                todo.append(k)
    return out


class Job:
    """What this run may stop: its steps' processes, found by MARK (in or out
    of the process group) and, for one that cleared its environment, as a
    descendant of a step seen while it ran and still in the group. When this
    run owns its process group (lockrun started it as its job, not nested in
    another job), also any other process left in the group."""

    def __init__(self, run_id, owns_group):
        self.run = run_id
        self.pgid = os.getpgid(0)
        self.owns_group = owns_group
        t = table()
        self.keep = {os.getpid()}
        p = os.getppid()
        while p in t:  # this coordinator's ancestors are never stopped
            self.keep.add(p)
            p = t[p][0]
            if p in self.keep or p <= 1:
                break

    def targets(self, token, seen):
        """Live processes to stop for `token` (the run's or a step's id), with `seen` pids."""
        t, m = table(), marks()
        out = {p for p, (ids, argv0) in m.items()
               if token in ids and os.path.basename(argv0) not in SHARED and p in t and not t[p][2]}
        out |= {p for p in seen if p in t and t[p][1] == self.pgid and not t[p][2]}
        if self.owns_group and token == self.run:
            out |= {p for p, (_, g, z) in t.items() if g == self.pgid and not z}
        return out - self.keep

    def stop(self, token, seen=frozenset(), grace=5.0):
        """SIGTERM, then SIGKILL, until no target is left. True if none is."""
        for sig, wait in ((signal.SIGTERM, grace), (signal.SIGKILL, 10.0)):
            alive = self.targets(token, seen)
            if not alive:
                return True
            for p in alive:
                try:
                    os.kill(p, sig)
                except ProcessLookupError:
                    pass
            end = time.monotonic() + wait
            while time.monotonic() < end:
                time.sleep(0.05)
                if not self.targets(token, seen):
                    return True
        return not self.targets(token, seen)


class Cancelled(Exception):
    pass


def start_step(job, step, index, logdir, env):
    log = os.path.join(logdir, re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9_.-]", "_", step["name"]) + ".log")
    lf = open(log, "wb")
    lf.write(("$ %s\n" % step["command"]).encode())
    lf.flush()
    # each step gets its own short scratch directory (socket paths must stay under
    # 104 bytes; steps of a group run at once)
    scratch = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cpt.", dir="/tmp")
    token = "%s.%d" % (job.run, index)
    ids = [x for x in env.get(MARK, "").split(":") if x] + [job.run, token]
    # no new session: the step stays in this job's process group
    p = subprocess.Popen(["bash", "-c", step["command"]], cwd=REPO, stdout=lf, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
                         stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, env=dict(env, TMPDIR=scratch, **{MARK: ":".join(ids)}))
    return {"step": step, "p": p, "lf": lf, "log": log, "t0": time.monotonic(), "timed_out": False,
            "scratch": scratch, "seen": {p.pid}, "token": token}


def finish_step(r):
    step, p = r["step"], r["p"]
    r["lf"].close()
    shutil.rmtree(r["scratch"], ignore_errors=True)
    secs = r.get("t1", time.monotonic()) - r["t0"]
    log = r["log"]
    out = open(log, "rb").read().decode("utf-8", "replace")
    # (counted without the "$ <command>" header line this runner wrote)
    body = out.split("\n", 1)[1] if "\n" in out else ""
    run, passed, failed, ignored = count(step, body)
    code, timed_out = p.returncode, r["timed_out"]
    ok = code == 0 and not timed_out and (step["kind"] == "build" or run >= step["least"]) and failed == 0
    ok = ok and not r.get("unstoppable")
    # a known failure: exactly the listed exit and the listed line, nothing else wrong
    kn = step.get("known")
    known_failure = bool(kn and code == kn["exit"] and not timed_out and not r.get("unstoppable")
                         and re.search(kn["regex"], body, re.M) and run >= step["least"])
    why = ("known pre-existing failure: %s" % kn["text"]) if known_failure else ("timed out after %g s" % step["limit"] if timed_out else "exit %s" % code if code != 0
           else "%d failed" % failed if failed else "processes it left could not be stopped" if r.get("unstoppable")
           else "ran %d tests, fewer than %d" % (run, step["least"]) if not ok else "")
    if r.get("leftovers"):
        why = (why + "; " if why else "") + "stopped %d leftover processes" % r["leftovers"]
    return {"name": step["name"], "kind": step["kind"], "command": step["command"], "limit": step["limit"],
            "least": step["least"], "group": step["group"], "exit": code, "seconds": round(secs, 2),
            "tests_run": run if step["kind"] != "build" else None,
            "passed": passed, "failed": failed, "ignored": ignored, "timed_out": timed_out, "ok": ok,
            "known_failure": known_failure, "known": kn, "why": why, "log": log, "log_sha256": sha256(log)}


def run_batch(job, batch, first, logdir, env):
    """Run steps at the same time (one step: alone); each has its own time limit."""
    running = []
    try:
        running = [start_step(job, s, first + i, logdir, env) for i, s in enumerate(batch)]
        last_scan = 0.0
        while True:
            now = time.monotonic()
            if now - last_scan > 0.25:
                t = table()
                for r in running:
                    if "t1" not in r:
                        r["seen"] |= descendants(r["p"].pid, t)
                last_scan = now
            for r in running:
                if "t1" in r:
                    continue
                if r["p"].poll() is not None:
                    r["t1"] = now
                elif now - r["t0"] > r["step"]["limit"]:
                    # this step's processes only: the others of its group go on
                    r["timed_out"] = True
                    if not job.stop(r["token"], r["seen"]):
                        r["unstoppable"] = True
                    r["p"].poll()
                    r["t1"] = time.monotonic()
            if all("t1" in r for r in running):
                break
            time.sleep(0.05)
        # leftovers: whatever the batch's steps left (marked, seen in the group, or
        # anything in a group this run owns)
        seen = set().union(*[r["seen"] for r in running])
        left = job.targets(job.run, seen)
        if left:
            stopped = job.stop(job.run, seen)
            for r in running:
                r["leftovers"] = len(left & r["seen"]) if len(running) > 1 else len(left)
                if not stopped:
                    r["unstoppable"] = True
        for r in running:
            if r["p"].returncode is None:
                r["p"].wait()
        return [finish_step(r) for r in running]
    except Cancelled:
        job.stop(job.run, set().union(*[r["seen"] for r in running]) if running else set(), grace=2.0)
        for r in running:
            r["lf"].close()
            shutil.rmtree(r["scratch"], ignore_errors=True)
        raise


def target_dir():
    """Cargo's target directory as cargo resolves it (None if cargo can't say)."""
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["cargo", "metadata", "--format-version", "1", "--no-deps"], cwd=REPO,
                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)
        return json.loads(out.stdout)["target_directory"] if out.returncode == 0 else None
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired):
        return None


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="scripts/test", description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
    ap.add_argument("--all", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--candidate")
    ap.add_argument("--summary")
    ap.add_argument("--logs")
    ap.add_argument("--list")
    ap.add_argument("--only", action="append", default=[])
    ap.add_argument("--phase", choices=("build", "check", "both"), default="both",
                    help="the build steps, the other steps, or both (default: two lockrun jobs, builds first)")
    ap.add_argument("--locked", action="store_true", help=argparse.SUPPRESS)  # set when run by lockrun
    a, rest = ap.parse_known_args()
    if a.candidate:
        if not a.all:
            ap.error("--candidate goes with --all")
        tool = os.path.join(REPO, "scripts", "test_candidate")
        os.execv(tool, [tool, a.candidate, *rest])
    if rest:
        ap.error("unknown arguments: %s" % " ".join(rest))
    mode = "all" if a.all else "fast"
    listfile = a.list or os.path.join(REPO, LISTS[mode])
    steps = read_list(listfile)  # (before taking the lock: a bad list costs nothing)
    if not a.locked and a.phase == "both":
        return run_both(a, mode, listfile, steps)
    if not a.locked:
        # one job of lockrun for the whole run. lockrun validates an inherited token
        # (nested in a real enclosing job: it runs us directly in that job's group)
        limit = OUTER_LIMIT
        lower = os.environ.get("SCRIPTS_TEST_OUTER_LIMIT")  # tests only; never above OUTER_LIMIT
        if lower:
            limit = min(limit, float(lower))
        lockrun = os.path.join(REPO, "scripts", "lockrun")
        os.execv(lockrun, [lockrun, "--timeout", "%g" % limit, "--owner", "scripts/test %s (%s)" % (mode, REPO),
                           "--", sys.executable, os.path.abspath(__file__), "--locked", *sys.argv[1:]])
    # --locked: only inside the lockrun job that runs us (its record names this process
    # group and our token): the leftover sweep stops every other process of the group
    lockdir = os.environ.get("LOCKRUN_DIR") or "/tmp/lockrun-%d" % os.getuid()
    try:
        rec = json.load(open(os.path.join(lockdir, "record.json")))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        rec = {}
    if not (os.environ.get("LOCKRUN_TOKEN") and rec.get("token") == os.environ["LOCKRUN_TOKEN"]
            and rec.get("state") == "running" and rec.get("pgid") == os.getpgid(0)):
        raise SystemExit("scripts/test: --locked is for the lockrun job that runs scripts/test; run it without --locked")
    # the job is ours alone if lockrun started it for this run: its leader (the trampoline)
    # is our parent and its command is this runner. Nested in another job (a batch, or
    # test_candidate's lockrun), the group holds that job's other processes too
    cmd = rec.get("command") or []
    owns = rec.get("pid") == os.getppid() and "--locked" in cmd and any(
        c.endswith("scripts/test") or os.path.abspath(c) == os.path.abspath(__file__) for c in cmd)
    job = Job(uuid.uuid4().hex[:16], owns)
    if a.phase != "both":
        steps = [st for st in steps if (st["kind"] == "build") == (a.phase == "build")]
    if a.only:
        missing = [n for n in a.only if n not in [s["name"] for s in steps]]
        if missing:
            raise SystemExit("scripts/test: no step named %s in %s" % (", ".join(missing), listfile))
        steps = [s for s in steps if s["name"] in a.only]
    logdir = a.logs or tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="claude-paint-test-%s-" % mode)
    os.makedirs(logdir, exist_ok=True)
    env = dict(os.environ)
    env.pop("EASEL_BOX", None)
    target = target_dir()
    if target:
        env["CARGO_TARGET_DIR"] = target
    started = datetime.datetime.now().astimezone().isoformat(timespec="seconds")
    wall0 = time.monotonic()
    results = []
    interrupted = False

    def on_signal(signum, frame):
        for s in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP, signal.SIGINT):
            signal.signal(s, signal.SIG_IGN)
        raise Cancelled()

    for s in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP, signal.SIGINT):
        signal.signal(s, on_signal)
    batches = []
    for s in steps:
        if s["group"] is not None and batches and batches[-1][0]["group"] == s["group"]:
            batches[-1].append(s)
        else:
            batches.append([s])
    try:
        first = 0
        for batch in batches:
            if len(batch) > 1:
                print("scripts/test: group %s: %s at the same time" % (batch[0]["group"], ", ".join(s["name"] for s in batch)), flush=True)
            else:
                print("scripts/test: %-34s ..." % batch[0]["name"], end="", flush=True)
            done = run_batch(job, batch, first, logdir, env)
            first += len(batch)
            for r in done:
                results.append(r)
                counts = "" if r["kind"] == "build" else "  %d run, %d failed%s" % (
                    r["tests_run"], r["failed"], ", %d ignored/skipped" % r["ignored"] if r["ignored"] else "")
                if len(batch) > 1:
                    print("scripts/test:   %-32s ..." % r["name"], end="")
                print(" %s %7.1f s%s%s" % ("ok  " if r["ok"] else "FAIL", r["seconds"], counts, "  (%s)" % r["why"] if r["why"] else ""), flush=True)
    except Cancelled:
        interrupted = True
        print("\nscripts/test: cancelled; the running steps were stopped", flush=True)
    good = all(r["ok"] or r["known_failure"] for r in results)
    verdict = ("unfinished" if interrupted or any(r["timed_out"] for r in results) or len(results) < len(steps)
               else "fail" if not good else "known_failure" if any(r["known_failure"] for r in results) else "pass")
    if a.only and verdict in ("pass", "known_failure"):
        verdict = "unfinished"  # a partial run is never a pass
    build = sum(r["seconds"] for r in results if r["kind"] == "build")
    tests = sum(r["seconds"] for r in results if r["kind"] != "build")
    summary = {
        "mode": mode, "phase": a.phase, "verdict": verdict, "verdict_text": verdict_text(verdict, results),
        "list": os.path.relpath(listfile, REPO),
        "list_sha256": sha256(listfile), "runner_sha256": sha256(os.path.abspath(__file__)),
        "target_dir": target, "only": a.only, "commit": git("rev-parse", "HEAD"),
        "dirty": bool(git("status", "--porcelain")), "started": started,
        "wall_seconds": round(time.monotonic() - wall0, 1), "build_seconds": round(build, 1),
        "test_seconds": round(tests, 1), "tests_run": sum(r["tests_run"] or 0 for r in results), "steps": results,
    }
    if a.summary:
        with open(a.summary, "w") as f:
            json.dump(summary, f, indent=1)
            f.write("\n")
    report(summary, logdir, "" if a.phase == "both" else " (%s phase)" % a.phase)
    if interrupted:
        return 130
    return EXIT[verdict]


# exit codes: pass 0; fail 1; a known pre-existing failure and nothing else wrong 4;
# unfinished 3 (a step timed out, or a partial run); cancelled 130; lockrun's timeout 124
EXIT = {"pass": 0, "fail": 1, "unfinished": 3, "known_failure": 4}


def verdict_text(verdict, results):
    if verdict == "known_failure":
        return "NOT ALL GREEN (known pre-existing failure: %s)" % "; ".join(
            r["known"]["text"] for r in results if r.get("known_failure"))
    return verdict.upper()


def report(summary, logdir, what=""):
    results = summary["steps"]
    bad = [r["name"] for r in results if not r["ok"]]
    print("scripts/test %s%s: %s. %d steps, %d tests in %.0f s (steps: build %.0f s, tests %.0f s); logs in %s%s" % (
        summary["mode"], what, summary["verdict_text"], len(results), summary["tests_run"], summary["wall_seconds"],
        summary["build_seconds"], summary["test_seconds"], logdir, "; not ok: " + ", ".join(bad) if bad else ""), flush=True)


def run_both(a, mode, listfile, steps):
    """The build steps, then the others: two lockrun jobs of OUTER_LIMIT each (the
    plan: builds and final check batches, ten minutes each). The check job runs only if
    every build passed. One summary for both, its steps in list order."""
    limit = OUTER_LIMIT
    lower = os.environ.get("SCRIPTS_TEST_OUTER_LIMIT")  # tests only; never above OUTER_LIMIT
    if lower:
        limit = min(limit, float(lower))
    lockrun = os.path.join(REPO, "scripts", "lockrun")
    logdir = a.logs or tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="claude-paint-test-%s-" % mode)
    work = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="claude-paint-test-phases-")
    rest = [x for x in sys.argv[1:]]
    for flag in ("--summary", "--logs"):
        while flag in rest:
            i = rest.index(flag)
            del rest[i:i + 2]
    rest = [x for x in rest if not x.startswith("--summary=") and not x.startswith("--logs=")]
    phases, parts = {}, []
    current, cancelled = [None], [False]

    def forward(signum, frame):  # cancelling this run cancels the lockrun job running now
        cancelled[0] = True
        if current[0] is not None and current[0].poll() is None:
            try:
                os.kill(current[0].pid, signum)
            except ProcessLookupError:
                pass

    for sg in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP, signal.SIGINT):
        signal.signal(sg, forward)
    for ph in ("build", "check"):
        if cancelled[0]:
            break
        out = os.path.join(work, ph + ".json")
        cmd = [lockrun, "--timeout", "%g" % limit, "--owner", "scripts/test %s %s (%s)" % (mode, ph, REPO), "--",
               sys.executable, os.path.abspath(__file__), "--locked", "--phase", ph, "--summary", out,
               "--logs", logdir, *rest]
        current[0] = subprocess.Popen(cmd)
        while True:
            try:
                code = current[0].wait()
                break
            except InterruptedError:
                continue
        current[0] = None
        if cancelled[0] and code == 0:
            code = 130
        try:
            part = json.load(open(out))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            part = None
        phases[ph] = {"limit": limit, "exit": code, "verdict": part["verdict"] if part else "unfinished",
                      "wall_seconds": part["wall_seconds"] if part else None}
        if part:
            parts.append(part)
        if code == 130 or not part or part["verdict"] not in ("pass", "known_failure"):
            break
    shutil.rmtree(work, ignore_errors=True)
    by_name = {r["name"]: r for p in parts for r in p["steps"]}
    results = [by_name[s["name"]] for s in steps if s["name"] in by_name]
    vs = [phases[ph]["verdict"] for ph in phases]
    verdict = ("unfinished" if "unfinished" in vs or len(phases) < 2 and vs[-1] != "fail" else "fail" if "fail" in vs
               else "known_failure" if "known_failure" in vs else "pass")
    if cancelled[0] or any(ph["exit"] == 130 for ph in phases.values()):
        verdict = "unfinished"
    if a.only and verdict in ("pass", "known_failure"):
        verdict = "unfinished"
    base = parts[0] if parts else {}
    summary = {
        "mode": mode, "phase": "both", "verdict": verdict, "verdict_text": verdict_text(verdict, results),
        "list": os.path.relpath(listfile, REPO), "list_sha256": sha256(listfile),
        "runner_sha256": sha256(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "target_dir": base.get("target_dir"), "only": a.only,
        "commit": git("rev-parse", "HEAD"), "dirty": bool(git("status", "--porcelain")),
        "started": base.get("started"), "phases": phases,
        "wall_seconds": round(sum(p["wall_seconds"] or 0 for p in phases.values()), 1),
        "build_seconds": round(sum(r["seconds"] for r in results if r["kind"] == "build"), 1),
        "test_seconds": round(sum(r["seconds"] for r in results if r["kind"] != "build"), 1),
        "tests_run": sum(r["tests_run"] or 0 for r in results), "steps": results,
    }
    if a.summary:
        with open(a.summary, "w") as f:
            json.dump(summary, f, indent=1)
            f.write("\n")
    report(summary, logdir, " (build and check phases)")
    if cancelled[0] or any(ph["exit"] == 130 for ph in phases.values()):
        return 130
    if any(ph["exit"] == 124 for ph in phases.values()):
        return 124
    return EXIT[verdict]


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
